So when the modal hides, `onModalHide` runs, and it schedules a focus 300ms later! 
Since `deleteContactMethod` triggers `Navigation.goBack()`, the transition takes about 300ms. 
So right as the transition finishes, the input gets focused, forcing the keyboard to open!

Wait, if the user clicks "Confirm" to delete, we are navigating back. Why should we refocus the input? 
We shouldn't! 
Proposal 4 says: "we are not focusing on input again after pressing cancel this will also make things consistent on all platforms"
Wait, if we don't focus on input after pressing *cancel*, is that correct? 
If the user cancels the deletion, they stay on the `ContactMethodDetailsPage`. The input should probably be refocused so they can continue typing. 
But if they confirm the deletion, they navigate away, so we shouldn't refocus. 
Wait, `onModalHide` runs regardless of whether they confirmed or cancelled! 
```javascript
            onModalHide={() => {
                InteractionManager.runAfterInteractions(() => {
                    validateCodeFormRef.current?.focusLastSelected?.();
                });
            }}
```
If they confirm, `toggleDeleteModal(false)` is called, which triggers `onModalHide`. 
If they cancel, `toggleDeleteModal(false)` is called, which triggers `onModalHide`. 
So `onModalHide` focuses the input in both cases! 

